Z||000000||Seanh||01-28-2001||03:13 PM||||U guy ever heard the Chineese cat food song? It goes to the tune of "Cats in the cradle and the silver spoon" Its a very funny song about Chinese resteraunts serving cat meat instead of chicken or fish. If you want it, email me and I'll send it to you. Its an mp3 @ about 1.5Mb.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||01-28-2001||04:06 PM||||There was a chinese place in town last year that the health dept closed down due to serving cat meat. Turned out some lady was eating whatever she had ordered, and noticed a piece of meat closely resembling a paw. She bagged it and had it x-rayed by the health dept. Healther dept was there the next day, performing a search, and they found what they were looking for. It's pretty gross what they found so I won't say, but that shop isn't here anymore.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||01-28-2001||04:15 PM||||Did that make national news? I think I heard about that a while back. Thats nasty! There is a local Chinese food place, I eat there alot and its really good. Guess I should look more closely at what I'm eating.||||reg||1
